# Local, gitignored list of patterns that must never be published.
#
# Copy this file to `.docs-leaks` and fill it in:
#
#   cp .docs-leaks.example .docs-leaks
#
# One regular expression per line, written WITHOUT slashes (they are compiled
# with `new RegExp(line, 'i')`, so matching is case-insensitive). Blank lines and
# lines starting with '#' are ignored. `npm run check:docs` reports every line of
# every documented file that matches one of them, and never prints the pattern.
#
# Typical entries for a self-hosted Discord bot:
#   - Discord ids: guild id, feed channel id, ids used in tests
#   - host paths: the stack directory, storage mounts, backup targets
#   - the real server aliases and labels used by your game servers
#   - real usernames that appear in examples or fixtures
#
# Examples (uncomment and adapt):
#   ^[0-9]{18,19}$
#   /opt/my-stack
#   /mnt/my-storage
#   my-minecraft-alias
